usage: evaluate_corrected.py [-h] --root ROOT --prompts PROMPTS
                             [--references REFERENCES]
                             [--reference-method REFERENCE_METHOD] [--res RES]
                             --out OUT [--metrics METRICS] [--device DEVICE]
                             [--bootstrap BOOTSTRAP]
                             [--bootstrap-seed BOOTSTRAP_SEED]
                             [--crop-seed CROP_SEED] [--crops CROPS]
                             [--threads THREADS] [--allow-missing]
                             [--no-wandb]
                             [--musiq-query-chunk MUSIQ_QUERY_CHUNK]
                             [--reference-clusters {rows,images}]

Evaluate completed sample PNG/JSON pairs and bootstrap by prompt.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --root ROOT           Root containing sample PNG files and JSON sidecars
  --prompts PROMPTS     Prompt JSONL with id and prompt
  --references REFERENCES
                        Reference JSONL with id and path
  --reference-method REFERENCE_METHOD
  --res RES             Optional resolution filter, for example 4096x4096
  --out OUT             Evaluation directory on scratch, also holds resumable
                        caches
  --metrics METRICS     all (HPSv3 optional) or comma list: clip,imagereward,p
                        ickscore,hpsv3,musiq,clipiqa,fid,kid,patch_fid,patch_k
                        id,spectrum,tiling
  --device DEVICE
  --bootstrap BOOTSTRAP
  --bootstrap-seed BOOTSTRAP_SEED
  --crop-seed CROP_SEED
  --crops CROPS         Fixed random 1024 crops per image, shared across
                        methods
  --threads THREADS
  --allow-missing       Exit successfully with explicitly reported unavailable
                        metrics
  --no-wandb            Disable W&B logging explicitly, useful for CPU
                        numerical tests
  --musiq-query-chunk MUSIQ_QUERY_CHUNK
                        Opt-in inference attention query chunking; preserves
                        native MUSIQ patches (0 disables)
  --reference-clusters {rows,images}
                        Bootstrap reference rows or shared image identities,
                        retaining every row's point-estimate weight
